REST style architecture :- (architectural principle of the web)
   1. States and functionalities are being devided into distributed resources.
   2.Every resource is  uniquely addressable and with uniform and minimium commands ( example- protocol-http, request type- GET/PUT/POST etc..)
   3.The protocol is client/ server, stateless and support caching.
   
   
   In HTTP request , request header contains 
   'Content-Type'='appplication/json' => data sent from client to server in JSON format.
   'Accept'='appication/XML' (or dataTyle in $.ajax)=> data sent from server to client in XML format. 
   
REST constrains:-
1.Client server -> In application , there should be client to send request and a server to response to the request.
2.Stateless-> Server should not store any information related to client. Hence each request can be treated as a new request 
              and hence stateless.
3. Cacheable:-  We can cache data that does not change frequently, so that client does not need to generate request each time.
4. Uniform Interface:- Any data that is requested by client is called resource. So for getting any resource, Web API exposes uniform 
                       URI (uniform resoure interface) .
                       
Http Verbs:
1.Get:- get request
2.Post- create new resource
3. Put- Update existing resource.
4. Delete- Delete a resource.

When to use WCF over Web API:-
    WCF needs lot more configuration to make it REST full, where as Web API is restfull by default.
    When any application needs to use protocol except http, then we should go with WCF. (in WCF we need to define two end points for same serviece.)
    
